lines += ['','These are sums of per-request waiting intervals, not wall-clock phase durations. Temporal overlap supports a dispatch-gate investigation; it is not independent causal attribution. It does not isolate network, disk force, GC or service execution, and overlapping categories must not be added. The zero same-producer overlap concerns these tail requests at 500/s; it does not rule out a client-window ceiling at higher rates.','','The measured CONTINUE post-offer p99 is 11.586/11.893 ms; global p99 is 66.299/67.375 ms. These percentiles are separate distributions and cannot be subtracted to invent a queue percentile. The original per-point analysis provides the actual recorded schedule-to-dispatch distributions. A 10 ms global target cannot be established merely by shortening maintenance while the observed post-offer p99 already exceeds it.','','The approximately one-second backlog sampler can miss short maintenance queues: a zero sampled maximum is not proof that no request waited. Raw per-arrival timestamps and per-worker high-water observations remain available. The console wording now makes this observation limit explicit.','','## Candidate work after the registered curve','','`RetentionAsyncMaintenanceV4.businessAllowed()` permits business in IDLE and, for CONTINUE, VERIFY_WAIT and FILE_WAIT. Its read turns hold an exclusive read bank. `RetentionBatchOwnerV3.openReadBank()` requires completed business/control closure, and `submit()` refuses business while the read bank is open. Simply relaxing the phase predicate would violate this ownership contract.','','A bounded experiment can yield to a limited business burst only between fully consumed and closed read banks, then drain those original tickets before opening the next bank. It must preserve history/event/byte credits, fixed cuts, exact original identities and deadlines, four-offer limits, full receipt verification and the before-ACK fence. New phases and burst budgets need explicit trace/auditor qualification and the same-artifact control comparison. This is a candidate, not an implemented or proven optimization.','','A larger alternative is an immutable prefix-export channel outside the replicated query path. Only the single writer may publish committed immutable bytes; the exporter must never read mutable engine state or influence replicated decisions through local reader state. Bound the current and active-reader buffers, connection count, payload bytes and original deadlines. Keep destructive ACKs on the replicated path after complete durable verification. This requires a new protocol and failure tests; no latency claim follows from the design.','','A smaller allocation candidate reuses an already encoded event-page reply for trace and persisted event data. It requires complete byte-equivalence checks and a controlled comparison. It cannot by itself establish the end-to-end target.','','[Complete derivation, input hashes and private raw references](../evidence/2026-10-26/runpod-cpu/async-capacity-v4/exact-cut-r2/rate-500-queue-diagnostic-r1/analysis/RESULT.json). The current fixed-configuration capacity curve remains the prerequisite for choosing the next candidate.','']
